abstract: >-
  A single-GPU, single-suite proof of concept for online RL fine-tuning of the
  flow-matching VLA SmolVLA using a Flow-SDE GRPO objective on LIBERO-Plus. The
  confirmatory result is a null: on a preregistered unseen-task evaluation, GRPO
  scored 20/138 against 19/138 for the SFT checkpoint it was initialized from
  (mean per-task difference +0.72 pp, 95% task-clustered bootstrap CI
  [-5.07, +6.52] pp, exact McNemar p = 1.0), which is "not established" under the
  decision rule fixed before the run. An earlier trained-task comparison is
  biased in favour of the arms trained on the collected rollouts and is not
  evidence of generalization. The repository documents two silent gradient
  pathologies (element-count ratio normalization and chunk-weighting bias), a
  staged privileged reward with a diagnostic funnel, a fully scripted Colab
  pipeline, and ships the preregistration and its amendment, the raw per-episode
  evaluation data with the scripts that recompute every reported number, and a
  runnable reproduction of an upstream LIBERO-Plus initial-state selection bug
  (huggingface/lerobot#4152). The manuscript is a separate, unfinished
  deliverable and is not part of this archive.
